{"id":"R0091","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Generic bit-wise computation task offloading; MASAC/MADDPG neural networks serve only as the optimizer with no distributed DNN inference workload.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1. Introduction","we first propose a multi-agent DRL (MADRL) approach","Primary research paper proposing a MADRL/MASAC method for joint task and energy offloading."],["E2","PDF",3,"3. Model description and problem formulation","M rotary-wing UAVs serve as the task owners","Evaluated setting explicitly models multiple UAVs (M in [3, 6] in Section 5.1 Table 2, p.8)."],["E3","PDF",3,"3. Model description and problem formulation (fn. 2)","the task mentioned in this paper is bit-wise","Checked Sections 3 (3.1-3.4), 4 (4.1-4.3), and 5 (5.1-5.2); workloads are generic bit-wise tasks without DNN inference."],["E3","PDF",4,"3.2. Task partitioning model","represents the data size of the computation task","Tasks are parameterized only by data size in bits and CPU cycles per bit rather than neural network layers or inference requests."],["E3","PDF",6,"4.2. MADDPG-based framework","used for the mapping from the current state","Fully-connected neural networks act solely as DRL actor/critic optimizers for partitioning and power control."],["E4","PDF",8,"5. Simulation results","comprehensive simulations are conducted to verify the performance","Provides quantitative simulation evaluation comparing MASAC against MADDPG, SAC, and DDPG."],["E5","PDF",1,"Article info","Accepted 13 June 2022 Available online 17 June 2022","Authoritative online publication date 2022-06-17 is within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","a joint task and energy offloading problem is","Full text (pp. 1-11) is in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Article info","Received 24 November 2021; Received in revised form","Full-text journal research article with revision/acceptance history in Computer Communications."],["E7","https://shop.elsevier.com/journals/computer-communications/0140-3664",0,"Journal description","Computer Communications is a peer-reviewed international journal that","Official Elsevier publisher page confirms Computer Communications is peer-reviewed."]]}
{"id":"R0099","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Centralized single-laptop processing of raw UAV RTSP streams; each feed runs independent YOLOv8n detection without multi-UAV or edge-cloud collaborative inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"I. Introduction","we propose a centralized UAV control architecture designed","Primary research report proposing a multithreaded UAV video processing and detection architecture."],["E2","PDF",8,"IV.B. Multithreaded Processing Performance","configurations of both single- and three-stream processing","Evaluated with three concurrent streams, each corresponding to an independent UAV feed (Fig. 1 p.7; Section IV.B p.8)."],["E3","PDF",6,"III.A. System Arcgitecture","Each UAV RTSP stream is independently managed by","Checked Sections III (A-C) and IV (A-E); each UAV stream is processed independently in a dedicated thread without cross-UAV fusion or distributed inference."],["E3","PDF",8,"IV.A. Experimental Setup","UAVs transmitted video streams to the ground station","UAVs only stream raw RTSP video to one centralized MSI laptop running YOLOv8n locally, with no UAV-to-UAV or edge-cloud DNN partitioning/orchestration."],["E4","PDF",8,"IV.A. Experimental Setup","The system was validated on a MSI laptop","Provides experimental evaluation of throughput, resource usage, reconnection recovery, and detection/tracking metrics."],["E5","PDF",1,"Header metadata","Volume 6, Issue 6, 2025 ISSN: 2715-5072","Publication year 2025 is wholly within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","Managing concurrent high-resolution video from multiple UAVs is","Full text (pp. 1-14) is in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Header metadata","Journal of Robotics and Control (JRC) Volume 6,","Full-text journal article with method and evaluation, but official JRC website (journal.umy.ac.id) was inaccessible to verify peer-review policy; remains U."]]}
{"id":"R0122","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Generic binary IoT-to-UAV task offloading optimized via K-means and SQP; collaborative inference is mentioned only as motivation with no DNN inference modeled or evaluated.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","We propose a confidence-calibrated hybrid trust framework that","Primary research paper proposing a hybrid trust model and penalty-guided optimization algorithm."],["E2","PDF",5,"4 Performance Evaluation and Discussion","with N=50 IoT devices and M=5 UAVs","Evaluates multi-UAV settings with 2 to 5 UAVs (Section 4, p.5)."],["E3","PDF",2,"2 System Model and Problem Formulation","They can offload computation-intensive tasks to their serving","Checked Sections 2 (2.1-2.3), 3, and 4; tasks are generic binary offloaded workloads characterized by data size, CPU cycles per bit, latency, and trust threshold."],["E3","PDF",4,"3 Proposed Optimization Framework","solved using sequential quadratic programming (SQP) [14], which","Method solves binary task association via K-means and SQP without any DNN/CNN/VLM/LLM inference execution, partitioning, or fusion."],["E4","PDF",5,"4 Performance Evaluation and Discussion","We evaluate the proposed framework via simulations with","Provides simulation evaluation comparing PGO against branch-and-bound, greedy, and baseline relaxation methods."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","Mobile Computing (MobiHoc '26), November 23-26, 2026, Tokyo,","Proceedings date November 23-26, 2026 is on or before the 2026-11-26 cutoff."],["E5","https://dblp.org/db/conf/mobihoc/mobihoc2026",0,"DBLP record footer","last updated on 2026-11-15 22:49 CET by the","Confirms MobiHoc 2026 proceedings metadata including this paper was available online before 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","Aerial edge computing brings Internet of things (IoT)","Full text (pp. 1-6) is in English."],["E7","https://cybernet2026.github.io/cybernet2026/",0,"Submission Instructions","For single-blind review, submissions must include the names","Official CyberNet 2026 (ACM MobiHoc 2026 workshop) page confirms single-blind peer review for 6-page technical papers with full method and evaluation."]]}
{"id":"R0126","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"F","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E1","secondary":["E7","E3"],"reason":"Book chapter (excluded under E1 and E7) synthesizing prior federated learning frameworks; the multi-UAV component (DECKS) performs federated training/weight aggregation rather than distributed DNN inference.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","This chapter presents a unified framework for decentralized","Book chapter synthesizing the authors' prior works [17, 18, 19, 24]; book chapters are excluded from primary synthesis under E1."],["E2","PDF",14,"3.4.3 UAVs knowledge sharing methodology","where a total of 10 UAVs cooperated under","DECKS evaluation explicitly models a multi-UAV swarm (5 and 10 cooperating UAVs)."],["E3","PDF",11,"3.4 DECKS architecture","enables UAV swarms to collaboratively train, fuse, and","Checked Sections 3.1-3.5 and 4; DECKS performs decentralized federated training across UAVs and relays trained models to vehicles rather than collaborative multi-UAV DNN inference."],["E3","PDF",13,"3.4.3 UAVs knowledge sharing methodology","each UAV updates its model locally and shares","Multi-UAV collaboration consists of local gradient training and 1-hop neighbor weight aggregation (federated learning)."],["E4","PDF",14,"3.4.3 UAVs knowledge sharing methodology","The DECKS framework was evaluated using a simulated","Reports simulation and testbed evaluations across Sections 3.2-3.5."],["E5","https://www.intechopen.com/chapters/1224598",0,"Chapter publication metadata","Reviewed: 04 July 2025 Published: 19 March 2026","Authoritative IntechOpen online publication date 2026-03-19 is within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","Autonomous systems deployed across robotics, transportation, and aerial","Full text (pp. 1-26) is in English."],["E7","PDF",22,"Copyright notice","This chapter is distributed under the terms of","Book chapter report type is ineligible under E7."]]}
{"id":"R0128","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"F","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"F","E5":"U","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E1","secondary":["E7","E2","E3","E4"],"reason":"Review article on visual semantic communication security without a proposed collaborative multi-UAV inference method or evaluation; exact 2026 online publication month/day is unverified.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","This paper reviews the role of semantic segmentation","Review/survey magazine article rather than a primary research contribution."],["E2","PDF",3,"III.A. Key Techniques (Table I note)","Quantitative metrics were empirically evaluated on the Cityscapes","No multi-UAV setting is evaluated; drone swarms are mentioned only in passing in the Abstract."],["E3","PDF",1,"I. Introduction","reviews relevant technological advancements, and discusses key aspects","Checked Sections II-IV; reviews semantic segmentation security mechanisms without proposing or evaluating multi-UAV collaborative DNN inference."],["E4","PDF",3,"III.A. Key Techniques","Table I presents a systematic comparison.","No proposed inference method is evaluated; Table I only benchmarks existing segmentation backbones on Cityscapes."],["E5","https://orcid.org/0009-0004-6829-6167",0,"Works (Crossref metadata)","2026 | Journal article","Only year 2026 is verifiable from PDF copyright/DOI and ORCID/Crossref; without exact month/day in cutoff year 2026 (download stamp excluded), E5 remains U."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","Semantic communication (SemCom) transcends traditional Shannon theory by","Full text (pp. 1-8) is in English."],["E7","https://ieee-ceda.org/publication/ieee-internet-things-magazine-iotm",0,"Publication description","The IEEE Internet of Things Magazine (IoTM) publishes","Although IEEE IoTM is peer-reviewed, this Early Access review article lacks a substantive proposed method and evaluation results required for research reports under E7."]]}
{"id":"R0142","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"F","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"F","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"F"},"primary":"E1","secondary":["E7","E2","E3","E4"],"reason":"Narrative overview/review paper on UAV swarm history, programs, and trends with no proposed method, no evaluated multi-UAV setting, no collaborative DNN inference, and no evaluation results.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",1,"Abstract","This paper combs the origin and development trend","Overview/review paper summarizing UAV swarm development rather than a primary research contribution."],["E2","PDF",4,"4.2.1 OFFSET Program","DARPA released the field test results of the","Discusses external historical swarm programs conceptually with no evaluated multi-UAV setting of its own in Sections 1-9."],["E3","PDF",3,"3.3 Emerging Convergence Technologies","will allow near real-time distributed inference and cross-domain","Checked Sections 1-9; distributed inference is mentioned only as a future trend with no inference method or workload."],["E4","PDF",8,"9 Conclusion","UAV swarm intelligence represents a transformative technological paradigm","Contains no experiments, simulations, emulations, or analytical performance evaluations anywhere in Sections 1-9."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","Intelligent Manufacturing (BDIM 2026), March 20-22, 2026, Jinan,","Official proceedings date March 20-22, 2026 is within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","UAV swarm operation has become a research hotspot","Full text (pp. 1-8) is in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"Abstract","systematically summarizes the latest research and development progress","Overview paper lacking both a defined method/system and evaluation results required under E7."]]}
{"id":"R0144","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"F","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"T"},"primary":"E2","secondary":["E3"],"reason":"Evaluates standalone onboard YOLOv5n video summarisation on a single custom UAV; multi-UAV swarm deployment is mentioned only as future work and no collaborative inference is performed.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",3,"Abstract","This paper introduces a modular UAV system for","Primary research paper proposing an onboard keyframe-summarisation and YOLOv5n detection pipeline."],["E2","PDF",5,"3.2 Hardware Architecture","A custom UAV was built using readily available","Evaluated hardware and pipeline use a single UAV."],["E2","PDF",9,"5 Conclusion and Future Work","Deploying a UAV swarm could enhance coverage and","Multi-UAV swarm deployment is explicitly deferred to future work, which does not satisfy E2."],["E3","PDF",6,"3.3 Video Summarisation Pipeline","The UAV runs a software pipeline that combines","Checked Sections 3 (3.1-3.4) and 4; standalone onboard YOLOv5n perception runs locally on one Raspberry Pi 4 without multi-UAV or edge-cloud collaborative inference."],["E3","PDF",7,"3.3.2 Proposed Flow","Transmission was simulated (copy-to-folder plus log) rather than","Only local detection and simulated MP4 copy-to-folder output are evaluated."],["E4","PDF",6,"3.3 Video Summarisation Pipeline","Testing was carried out on both a Raspberry","Provides empirical runtime, CPU, file-size, detection-retention, and battery energy evaluations."],["E5","PDF",3,"ACM Reference Format","the Internet of Things (IOT 2025), November 18-21, 2025,","Proceedings date November 18-21, 2025 (and ACM DL cover Published: 18 November 2025 on p.2) is within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26."],["E6","PDF",3,"Abstract","Rapid detection of individuals in search and rescue","Full text (pp. 3-9) is in English."],["E7","https://iot-conference.org/iot2025/call-for-papers/",0,"Important dates","Papers will be peer-reviewed by at least three","Official IoT 2025 CFP confirms double-blind peer review by at least three TPC experts for ACM DL research papers."]]}
{"id":"R0148","access":"READ","decision":"EXCLUDE","criteria":{"E1":"T","E2":"T","E3":"F","E4":"T","E5":"T","E6":"T","E7":"U"},"primary":"E3","secondary":[],"reason":"Generic indivisible MEC task offloading where a lightweight DNN is used solely as the offloading-decision optimizer, with no distributed DNN inference workload.","evidence":[["E1","PDF",2,"1 Introduction","We propose an energy-aware optimization framework, called Offloading-Deployment","Primary research paper proposing the two-stage ODE task offloading and UAV deployment framework."],["E2","PDF",6,"4 Experimental results and analysis","The number of UAVs is fixed at 5,","Evaluates multi-UAV MEC scenarios with 3 to 7 UAVs (Section 4, pp. 6-7)."],["E3","PDF",4,"2.5 Problem Formulation","each task is indivisible and must be processed","Checked Sections 2 (2.1-2.5), 3 (3.1-3.3), and 4; workloads are generic indivisible tasks defined by CPU cycles, data size, and delay deadline."],["E3","PDF",4,"3 The ODE Framework","a deep neural network (DNN) generates the offloading","The DNN serves solely as an optimizer predicting binary offloading decisions, followed by Differential Evolution for UAV placement, with no DNN inference workload."],["E4","PDF",6,"4 Experimental results and analysis","To evaluate the effectiveness of the ODE algorithm,","Provides simulation evaluation of timeout rate, overdue users, and energy cost against five baselines."],["E5","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","Computer Applications (BDCTA 2026), February 06-08, 2026, Harbin,","Official proceedings date February 06-08, 2026 is within 2021-01-01 through 2026-11-26."],["E5","https://www.bdcta.org/2026",0,"The Successful Conclusion of BDCTA 2026","On February 7, 2026, 2026 2nd International Conference","Official BDCTA 2026 site confirms the conference took place in February 2026 before the 2026-11-26 cutoff."],["E6","PDF",1,"Abstract","With the explosive growth of Internet of Things","Full text (pp. 1-8) is in English."],["E7","PDF",1,"ACM Reference Format","ACM, New York, NY, USA, 8 pages.","Full-text 8-page ACM proceedings paper with method and evaluation, but official peer-review policy text was unavailable from ACM DL or bdcta.org/2026; remains U."]]}
